    // DORA page
    'compliance.dora.seo.title': 'DORA Compliance with Bug Bounty | Defend Denmark',
    'compliance.dora.seo.description': 'How Defend Denmark satisfies DORA Articles 24, 25, and 45 through continuous, crowdsourced security testing for EU financial entities. Article-by-article mapping of deliverables.',
    'compliance.dora.hero.title': 'DORA',
    'compliance.dora.hero.subtitle': 'Continuous, evidence-driven security testing that maps directly to DORA Articles 24, 25, and 45 — and prepares you for Threat-Led Penetration Testing under Article 26.',
    'compliance.dora.what.title': 'What is DORA?',
    'compliance.dora.what.body': 'DORA is the EU regulation on digital operational resilience for the financial sector. It has been in force since 17 January 2025 and applies to banks, insurers, investment firms, payment institutions, crypto-asset service providers, and the critical ICT third-party providers that serve them.',

    'compliance.dora.req.intro': 'DORA Chapters II and IV impose specific testing and vulnerability-management duties on financial entities. The articles most relevant to ongoing security testing are:',
    'compliance.dora.req.1.article': 'Article 6',
    'compliance.dora.req.1.title': 'ICT risk management framework',
    'compliance.dora.req.1.body': 'Financial entities must establish a sound, comprehensive and well-documented ICT risk management framework covering identification, protection, detection, response, and recovery.',
    'compliance.dora.req.2.article': 'Article 24',
    'compliance.dora.req.2.title': 'General requirements for digital operational resilience testing',
    'compliance.dora.req.2.body': 'Establishes a sound, comprehensive digital operational resilience testing programme as an integral part of the ICT risk management framework, with risk-based methodologies and full documentation.',
    'compliance.dora.req.3.article': 'Article 25',
    'compliance.dora.req.3.title': 'Testing of ICT tools and systems',
    'compliance.dora.req.3.body': 'Tests of ICT tools and systems must include vulnerability assessments and scans, open-source analyses, network security assessments, gap analyses, physical security reviews, source code reviews, scenario-based tests, compatibility testing, performance testing, end-to-end testing, and penetration testing — appropriate to risk.',
    'compliance.dora.req.4.article': 'Article 26-27',
    'compliance.dora.req.4.title': 'Advanced testing — Threat-Led Penetration Testing (TLPT)',
    'compliance.dora.req.4.body': 'Designated entities carry out TLPT at least every three years, following the TIBER-EU framework, executed by qualified internal or external testers meeting Article 27 requirements.',
    'compliance.dora.req.5.article': 'Article 45',
    'compliance.dora.req.5.title': 'Information-sharing arrangements on cyber threat information',
    'compliance.dora.req.5.body': 'Financial entities may exchange cyber threat information and intelligence — including indicators of compromise and tactics — within trusted communities to enhance digital operational resilience.',
    'compliance.dora.req.6.article': 'Article 13',
    'compliance.dora.req.6.title': 'Learning and evolving',
    'compliance.dora.req.6.body': 'Entities must monitor the effectiveness of their digital operational resilience strategy, capture lessons from tests and incidents, and feed them back into the ICT risk management framework.',

    'compliance.dora.coverage.intro': 'Each Defend Denmark deliverable below maps directly to a DORA article. Our reports are structured so you can hand them to Finanstilsynet and point at the specific obligation each artefact satisfies.',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.1.article': 'Article 6 — ICT risk management framework',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.1.how': 'Continuous crowdsourced testing produces ongoing identification, detection, and response evidence across all in-scope ICT systems. Findings are classified by severity, asset, and CWE so they slot directly into your risk register.',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.2.article': 'Article 24 — Resilience testing programme',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.2.how': 'Defend Denmark functions as a documented testing programme: scope, methodology, frequency, and risk-prioritised coverage are captured in writing. Annual programme summaries are produced for regulator review.',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.3.article': 'Article 25 — Testing of ICT tools and systems',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.3.how': 'We deliver the testing methodologies named in Article 25 in a continuous form: vulnerability assessments, scans, network security assessments, source code reviews (where in scope), scenario-based tests, and penetration testing — performed by verified ethical hackers across the year, not as a one-off audit.',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.4.article': 'Article 26 — Preparing for TLPT',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.4.how': 'For designated entities subject to TLPT, our continuous coverage hardens assets and surfaces issues before the threat-led engagement begins. We do not replace TLPT (which requires Article 27 testers); we reduce its findings and improve its outcome.',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.5.article': 'Article 45 — Cyber threat information sharing',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.5.how': 'Our coordinated vulnerability disclosure channel between researchers and your security team is itself an Article 45 information-sharing arrangement. Findings, indicators, and remediation guidance flow into your trusted-community processes.',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.6.article': 'Article 13 — Learning and evolving',
    'compliance.dora.coverage.6.how': 'Periodic executive summaries — MTTR by severity, finding density, CWE distribution, retest outcomes — give you the lessons-learned input that Article 13 expects, ready to feed back into the ICT risk framework.',

    'compliance.dora.evidence.1': 'Per-finding reports with CVSS-based severity, reproduction steps, affected assets, and remediation guidance.',
    'compliance.dora.evidence.2': 'Triage timestamps and SLA evidence demonstrating continuous coverage across the testing year.',
    'compliance.dora.evidence.3': 'Remediation tracking and re-test validation per Article 24(5) internal validation expectations.',
    'compliance.dora.evidence.4': 'Annual digital operational resilience testing programme summary aligned with Article 24.',
    'compliance.dora.evidence.5': 'Periodic executive attestations suitable for board reporting and supervisory dialogue.',
    'compliance.dora.evidence.6': 'Aggregated metrics: coverage, MTTR, finding distribution by severity, asset class, and vulnerability type (CWE).',

    'compliance.dora.local.title': 'Denmark',
