    'compliance.nis2.hero.subtitle': 'Article-by-article coverage of vulnerability handling, coordinated disclosure, and effectiveness assessment for essential and important entities across all 18 covered sectors.',
    'compliance.nis2.what.title': 'What is NIS2?',
    'compliance.nis2.what.body': 'NIS2 is the EU directive that significantly expands cybersecurity obligations across the union. It is transposed into Danish law as NIS2-loven and reaches "essential" and "important" entities in 18 sectors — including energy, transport, healthcare, digital infrastructure, public administration, manufacturing, and food.',

    'compliance.nis2.req.intro': 'NIS2 places concrete cybersecurity, vulnerability-handling, and disclosure duties on essential and important entities. The articles most relevant to ongoing security testing are:',
    'compliance.nis2.req.1.article': 'Article 12',
    'compliance.nis2.req.1.title': 'Coordinated vulnerability disclosure and a European vulnerability database',
    'compliance.nis2.req.1.body': 'Member States designate a CSIRT as coordinator for coordinated vulnerability disclosure. ENISA operates a European vulnerability database to enable Union-wide sharing of vulnerability information.',
    'compliance.nis2.req.2.article': 'Article 21(1)',
    'compliance.nis2.req.2.title': 'Cybersecurity risk-management measures',
    'compliance.nis2.req.2.body': 'Essential and important entities must take appropriate and proportionate technical, operational, and organisational measures to manage the risks posed to the security of network and information systems.',
    'compliance.nis2.req.3.article': 'Article 21(2)(b)',
    'compliance.nis2.req.3.title': 'Incident handling',
    'compliance.nis2.req.3.body': 'Entities must put in place documented processes for incident handling, including detection, analysis, containment, and response.',
    'compliance.nis2.req.4.article': 'Article 21(2)(e)',
    'compliance.nis2.req.4.title': 'Security in network and information systems acquisition, development and maintenance — including vulnerability handling and disclosure',
    'compliance.nis2.req.4.body': 'Entities must operate processes for vulnerability handling and disclosure as part of securing the systems they acquire, develop, and maintain.',
    'compliance.nis2.req.5.article': 'Article 21(2)(f)',
    'compliance.nis2.req.5.title': 'Policies and procedures to assess effectiveness of cybersecurity risk-management measures',
    'compliance.nis2.req.5.body': 'Entities must adopt policies and procedures — for example, regular testing — to assess the effectiveness of their cybersecurity risk-management measures.',
    'compliance.nis2.req.6.article': 'Article 23',
    'compliance.nis2.req.6.title': 'Reporting obligations',
    'compliance.nis2.req.6.body': 'Significant incidents must be notified to the CSIRT or competent authority — early warning within 24 hours, incident notification within 72 hours, and a final report within one month.',

    'compliance.nis2.coverage.intro': 'Each Defend Denmark deliverable below maps directly to a NIS2 article. Our reports are designed to be presentable as evidence to a Danish supervisor — point at the relevant article, hand over the artefact.',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.1.article': 'Article 12 — Coordinated vulnerability disclosure',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.1.how': 'Defend Denmark operates as your coordinated vulnerability disclosure (CVD) intake — verified researchers submit, we triage, you receive structured reports. The programme is aligned with the Member State CVD policy and feeds the ENISA European vulnerability database where applicable.',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.2.article': 'Article 21(2)(e) — Vulnerability handling and disclosure',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.2.how': 'A documented, audit-ready vulnerability handling programme: researcher submission, classification, severity scoring, remediation tracking, and retest validation. The programme itself is the evidence Article 21(2)(e) asks for.',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.3.article': 'Article 21(2)(f) — Effectiveness assessment',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.3.how': 'Continuous testing produces effectiveness metrics — MTTR by severity, finding density over time, retest pass-rate, coverage breadth. These are exactly the "policies and procedures to assess effectiveness" the article requires.',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.4.article': 'Article 21(2)(b) — Incident handling input',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.4.how': 'Per-finding reports include reproduction steps, severity, and discovery timestamps — directly usable as input to your incident handling process when a finding crosses the significance threshold.',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.5.article': 'Article 23 — Notification timeline support',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.5.how': 'Findings reach you with timestamps that support the 24h early warning and 72h incident notification timelines. Notification to the CSIRT remains your responsibility; the time-to-discovery evidence is in our reports.',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.6.article': 'Article 21(1) — Risk-management measures',
    'compliance.nis2.coverage.6.how': 'Coverage reports demonstrate that the technical measure of continuous third-party testing has been adopted in proportion to the risk profile of your network and information systems.',

