    'compliance.nis2.local.title': 'Denmark',
    'compliance.nis2.local.body': 'In Denmark, NIS2-loven is supervised by Digitaliseringsstyrelsen within the digital sector in Denmark. Our disclosure programme and audit-ready reports are designed to slot into the documentation a Danish supervisor expects to see.',

    // CRA page
    'compliance.cra.seo.title': 'Cyber Resilience Act Compliance | Defend Denmark',
    'compliance.cra.seo.description': 'Defend Denmark satisfies CRA Article 13 manufacturer obligations and Annex I Part II vulnerability handling requirements through continuous discovery, CVD policy operation, and conformity-assessment-ready documentation.',
    'compliance.cra.hero.title': 'CRA',
    'compliance.cra.hero.subtitle': 'Article-by-article coverage of manufacturer obligations and Annex I vulnerability handling for any product with digital elements sold in the EU.',
    'compliance.cra.what.title': 'What is the Cyber Resilience Act?',
    'compliance.cra.what.body': 'The CRA is the EU regulation that entered into force in December 2024, with main obligations applying from December 2027. It covers any product with digital elements sold in the EU — IoT devices, software, hardware with connectivity — and applies to manufacturers, importers, and distributors.',

    'compliance.cra.req.intro': 'CRA combines essential cybersecurity requirements (Annex I) with manufacturer duties (Article 13), reporting obligations (Article 14), and a documentation regime (Article 31) that feeds the conformity assessment route to CE marking. The articles most relevant to ongoing security testing are:',
    'compliance.cra.req.1.article': 'Article 6 + Annex I Part I',
    'compliance.cra.req.1.title': 'Essential cybersecurity requirements for products with digital elements',
    'compliance.cra.req.1.body': 'Products must be designed, developed, and produced to ensure an appropriate level of cybersecurity based on risks — including being delivered without known exploitable vulnerabilities and protected from unauthorised access.',
    'compliance.cra.req.2.article': 'Article 13',
    'compliance.cra.req.2.title': 'Obligations of manufacturers',
    'compliance.cra.req.2.body': 'Manufacturers must operate vulnerability handling processes throughout the support period, including a coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy and a single point of contact for reporting vulnerabilities.',
    'compliance.cra.req.3.article': 'Annex I Part II',
    'compliance.cra.req.3.title': 'Vulnerability handling requirements',
    'compliance.cra.req.3.body': 'Identify and document vulnerabilities; address them without delay through security updates; perform regular tests and reviews; share information about fixed vulnerabilities; operate a coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy.',
    'compliance.cra.req.4.article': 'Article 14',
    'compliance.cra.req.4.title': 'Reporting obligations of manufacturers',
    'compliance.cra.req.4.body': 'Actively exploited vulnerabilities and severe incidents must be reported to ENISA — early warning within 24 hours, full notification within 72 hours, and final report within 14 days.',
    'compliance.cra.req.5.article': 'Article 31',
    'compliance.cra.req.5.title': 'Technical documentation',
    'compliance.cra.req.5.body': 'Manufacturers must draw up and keep technical documentation demonstrating conformity with the essential requirements — including the cybersecurity risk assessment and the vulnerability handling processes.',
    'compliance.cra.req.6.article': 'Article 32',
    'compliance.cra.req.6.title': 'Conformity assessment procedures',
    'compliance.cra.req.6.body': 'Before placing a product on the market, manufacturers carry out a conformity assessment to demonstrate fulfilment of the essential requirements — the route depending on whether the product is default, important, or critical.',

    'compliance.cra.coverage.intro': 'Each Defend Denmark deliverable below maps directly to a CRA article or Annex I requirement. Our outputs are produced in a form that goes straight into your technical documentation file and conformity assessment.',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.1.article': 'Article 13 + Annex I Part II.5 — Coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.1.how': 'Defend Denmark provides the documented CVD policy and operates the single point of contact for reporting vulnerabilities. Researcher submissions are received, triaged, and tracked under your name — directly satisfying the manufacturer obligation.',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.2.article': 'Annex I Part II.1 — Identify and document vulnerabilities',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.2.how': 'Continuous external vulnerability discovery by verified ethical hackers throughout the product support period. Each finding is documented with affected component, version, severity, and reproduction steps.',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.3.article': 'Annex I Part II.2 — Address without delay',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.3.how': 'Per-finding reports include exploitability assessment and concrete remediation guidance, enabling your engineering team to issue timely security updates within the support period.',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.4.article': 'Annex I Part II.3 — Regular tests and reviews',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.4.how': 'The Defend Denmark programme is itself an ongoing test-and-review regime — broader than periodic pentests and proportionate to the risk profile of the product. Coverage reports demonstrate the regularity.',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.5.article': 'Annex I Part II.6 — Information sharing about vulnerabilities',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.5.how': 'Aggregated and per-finding reporting feeds your information-sharing obligations and supports the customer-facing communication of fixed vulnerabilities.',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.6.article': 'Article 14 — 24h ENISA reporting timeline',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.6.how': 'Severity-classified, time-stamped findings give you the early-warning signal needed to meet the 24h ENISA notification window for actively exploited issues. Notification itself remains the manufacturer\'s act; we provide the discovery evidence and timeline.',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.7.article': 'Article 31 — Technical documentation',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.7.how': 'Per-finding reports, remediation evidence, retest validation, and the CVD policy documentation are produced in a form that goes straight into the technical documentation file.',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.8.article': 'Article 32 — Conformity assessment',
    'compliance.cra.coverage.8.how': 'Programme summaries and coverage reports are usable as evidence of effective vulnerability handling within the conformity assessment route — whether internal control (default) or third-party assessment (important / critical).',

    'compliance.cra.evidence.1': 'Documented Coordinated Vulnerability Disclosure (CVD) policy meeting Article 13 and Annex I Part II.5.',
    'compliance.cra.evidence.2': 'Single point of contact for vulnerability reporting, operated by Defend Denmark on the manufacturer\'s behalf.',
    'compliance.cra.evidence.3': 'Per-finding reports — affected component, severity, reproduction steps, remediation guidance, retest evidence.',
